$DIR/main.p:9:9: cannot return alloc.Use(&a), which points into a, a local variable of install
    alloc.Use(&a) points into a. a is a local variable of install (declared at
    main.p:8). Its memory is reclaimed when install returns, so alloc.Use(&a)
    would point at memory that no longer holds a.
    Go would move this memory to the heap, and its garbage collector would free
    it later. Plutonium has no garbage collector and never moves memory to the
    heap behind the program's back, so that every allocation is visible in the
    code.
    Return values instead of views of a, or allocate a and return its owner, an
    owned[pluto/arena.Fixed]:
        a := new(pluto/arena.Fixed)
        ...
        return a
    (see "Views" in the Plutonium spec, section 18.3)
    (run "pluto explain E3001" for a longer explanation)
